message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software and the accompanying paper."
title: "SPNN-QVI: Scaled Projection Neural Network for Quasi-Variational Inequalities"
abstract: >-
  Julia implementation of a scaled projection neural network for
  quasi-variational inequalities with state-dependent constraint set
  S(x) = m(x) + S and fixed symmetric positive-definite matrix M.
  Integrates the continuous-time dynamics
  dx/dt = lambda * [P_{S(x),M^{-1}}(x - alpha * M * F(x)) - x]
  (projection in the M^{-1} metric) by adaptive ODE integration
  (OrdinaryDiffEq.jl) and by a discrete Krasnosel'skii-Mann iteration;
  sparse obstacle-type projections are computed by a KKT-verified
  primal-dual active-set method.
